<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>I told you that story=E2=80=99s an elaboratio=
n of this line: "And God saw that the wickedness of man was great in the ea=
rth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil =
continually." It=E2=80=99s a question worth asking: just exactly what are y=
our motives? Well, maybe they=E2=80=99re purer than mine were, and it=E2=80=
=99s certainly possible. I don=E2=80=99t think that I=E2=80=99m naturally a=
 particularly good person. I think I have to work at it very, very hard. I =
don=E2=80=99t necessarily think that everyone is like that. But some people=
 are worse than that, and everyone=E2=80=99s like that, to some degree.=20
<br><br>So it=E2=80=99s worth thinking about: just how much trouble are you=
 trying to cause? The other thing you might think about is, if you=E2=80=99=
re not doing something important with your life, by your own definition=E2=
=80=94because that=E2=80=99s the game that we=E2=80=99re playing, and you g=
et to define the terms, at least initially=E2=80=94maybe you=E2=80=99re pro=
ne to cause trouble, just because you don=E2=80=99t have anything better to=
 do. Trouble is more interesting than boring. That=E2=80=99s something you =
learn if you read Dostoevsky. Dostoevsky knew that extraordinarily well. An=
d so if you=E2=80=99re not pushing yourself to the limits of your capacity,=
 then you have plenty of leftover willpower, energy, and resources to devot=
e to causing interesting trouble. I would also say that this is an archetyp=
al scenario: "And God saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth=
, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil con=
tinually." That=E2=80=99s something to meditate on.=20
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s not self-destructive, because it=E2=80=99s like the di=
agnosis of an illness. It=E2=80=99s like, if that does happen to be the cas=
e for you, to some degree=E2=80=94maybe it=E2=80=99s only 10 percent of you=
, or maybe it=E2=80=99s 90 percent=E2=80=94well, then coming to terms with =
that is excellent, because, maybe, you can stop doing it. What would be the=
 downside to that? You=E2=80=99d have to give up your resentment, hatred, a=
nd all of that, obviously. That=E2=80=99s annoying, because those emotions =
are easy to engage in, and they=E2=80=99re engaging, and they have a feelin=
g of self-righteousness with them. But you=E2=80=99re not doing this to put=
 yourself down: you=E2=80=99re doing this to separate the wheat from the ch=
aff and to leave everything that you don=E2=80=99t have to be, behind.<inpu=
