<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>"And it repented the Lord that he had made ma=
n on the earth, and it grieved him at his heart. And the Lord said, I will =
destroy man whom I have created from the face of the earth; both man, and b=
east, and the creeping thing, and the fowls of the air; for it repenteth me=
 that I have made them."
<br><br>What=E2=80=99s the idea? Well, the idea is that the cosmos that God=
 created had become corrupt. That=E2=80=99s a funny thing about Genesis tha=
t always hits me, is that that=E2=80=99s also true. I told you that the Mes=
opotamians believed that human beings were made out of the blood of <a href=
=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20181221012830/https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Kingu" target=3D"_blank"><span class=3D"blueText">Kingu</span></a>, who w=
as the worst monster that the dragon of chaos could imagine. That=E2=80=99s=
 a pretty harsh diagnosis. But the reason the Mesopotamians believed that i=
s because they knew=E2=80=94as did the authors of Genesis=E2=80=94that huma=
n beings are the only creatures in the cosmos of being who are actually cap=
able of conscious deceit and malevolence. The question is, to what degree d=
oes the expression of that conscious deceit and malevolence corrupt things =
so badly that it would be better that they didn=E2=80=99t exist at all?
<br><br>There=E2=80=99s a story associated with a flood in the <a href=3D"h=
ttps://web.archive.org/web/20181221012830/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epi=
c_of_Gilgamesh" target=3D"_blank"><span class=3D"blueText">Epic of Gilgames=
h</span></a> that has exactly the same underlying narrative structure. In f=
act, some people think that the story of Noah was derived from it. The Gods=
, who repented of their creation, determined that erasing it would be bette=
r than allowing it to propagate. You see the same thing in the Mesopotamian=
 creation myth, the <a href=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20181221012830/h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/En%C3%BBma_Eli%C5%A1" target=3D"_blank"><span =
class=3D"blueText">Enuma Elis</span></a>. The early Gods, who are represent=
ative of the giants of humanity, I would say, make so much noise, and are s=
o careless, that the original creator God, Tiamat, decides to wipe them fro=
m the face of the earth.=20
<br><br>When you read something like this, if you read it from an informed,=
 historical perspective, it starts to have a depth that makes it transcend =
this archaic and fairytale-like element of the story. I=E2=80=99ve read som=
e very terrible things about what happened in Nazi Germany, and what happen=
ed when the Japanese invaded China, and just what happened generally in the=
 history of mankind. Things can get so bad that it takes the imagination of=
 a very bad person to conceptualize them. When they get that bad, this is t=
he only kind of language that works to describe them.=20
<br><br>That=E2=80=99s another thing that I=E2=80=99ve discovered by workin=
g with my clinical clients: when their lives are really not going well=E2=
=80=94when they=E2=80=99re close to suicide, or when they=E2=80=99re close =
to homicide, or when there are things going on in the family that are so co=
rrupt and terrible that they reach back generations and are aimed at nothin=
g but misery and destruction=E2=80=94the only language that suffices has a =
religious tone. There=E2=80=99s nothing else available to describe what=E2=
=80=99s happening with the proper level of seriousness. It might be that yo=
u=E2=80=99ve never encountered a situation that required that level of seri=
ousness. But that doesn=E2=80=99t mean that those situations don=E2=80=99t =
exist. They exist. You generally do everything you can to avoid being ensco=
nced in them, but they certainly do exist. The probability that you=E2=80=
=99ll encounter a situation like that, or two, at some point in your life i=
s extraordinarily high. You=E2=80=99ll tangle with someone who=E2=80=99s ma=
levolent right to the core, and maybe it=E2=80=99ll be you that is malevole=
nt. That=E2=80=99ll be a big shock. And then these poetic descriptors start=
 to become much more real.<input class=3D"spoilerbutton" type=3D"button" va=
lue=3D"OPEN SLIDE"><div class=3D"spoiler">
