<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>Those are famous lines, and that=E2=80=99s so=
rt of Christ the hippy. It=E2=80=99s like, hey, let it all hang out=E2=80=
=94that=E2=80=99s an old phrase. Do your thing, and everything will come to=
 you. These lines have been interpreted in that manner many times. But that=
=E2=80=99s seriously not the proper interpretation, because there=E2=80=99s=
 a kicker with this injunction. The kicker is this: "for your heavenly Fath=
er knoweth that ye have need of all these things. But seek ye first the kin=
gdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unt=
o you."
<br><br>That=E2=80=99s a lot different than the hippy thing, right? There=
=E2=80=99s a very, very, very interesting idea, here. It=E2=80=99s certainl=
y one of the most profound ideas that I=E2=80=99ve ever encountered. The id=
ea is that, if you configure your life so that what you are genuinely doing=
 is aiming at the highest possibly good, then the things that you need to s=
urvive and thrive on a day-to-day basis will deliver themselves to you. Tha=
t=E2=80=99s a hypothesis, and it=E2=80=99s not some simple hypothesis. What=
 it basically says is, if you dare to do the most difficult thing that you =
can conceptualize, your life will work out better than it will if you do an=
ything else. Well, how are you going to find out if that=E2=80=99s true?=20
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s a <a href=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/2018122101283=
0/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B8ren_Kierkegaard" target=3D"_blank"><=
span class=3D"blueText">Kierkegaardian</span></a> leap of faith. There=E2=
=80=99s no way you=E2=80=99re going to find out whether or not that=E2=80=
=99s true unless you do it. No one can tell you, either: working for someon=
e else is no proof that it will work for you. You have to be all-in in this=
 game. The idea is, "seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousnes=
s." It=E2=80=99s like, that=E2=80=99s actually a fairly important caution w=
hen you=E2=80=99re talking about not having to pay attention to what you=E2=
=80=99re going to eat or what you=E2=80=99re going to wear. What it=E2=80=
=99s essentially saying is that those problems are trivial in comparison. T=
he probability=E2=80=94if you manifest yourself properly in the world=E2=80=
=94that those things will come your way is extraordinarily high. I believe =
that=E2=80=99s exactly right. I=E2=80=99ve watched people operate in the wo=
rld, and I would say that there is no more effective way of operating in th=
e world than to conceptualize the highest good that you can and then strive=
 to attain it. There=E2=80=99s no more practical pathway to the kind of suc=
cess that you could have if you actually knew what success was. That=E2=80=
=99s what this sermon is attempting to posit.=20
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s like in the story of Pinocchio. What happens at the be=
ginning of the story of Pinocchio is that Geppetto wishes on a star. We tal=
ked about that a little bit. Geppetto aligns himself with the metaphorical =
manifestation of the highest good he can conceptualize. He makes a commitme=
nt, let=E2=80=99s say. He aims at the star. For him, the star is the possib=
ility that he can take his creation=E2=80=94a puppet, whose strings are bei=
ng pulled by unseen forces=E2=80=94and have it transform into something tha=
t=E2=80=99s autonomous and real. Well, that=E2=80=99s a hell of an ambition=
. We=E2=80=99re wise enough to put that in a children=E2=80=99s movie but t=
oo foolish to understand what it means.=20
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s such an interesting juxtaposition that we can both kno=
w that and not know it at the same time. You can go to the movie; you can w=
atch it, and it makes sense. But that doesn=E2=80=99t mean that you can go =
home, and think, I know what that meant. Well, people are complicated. We e=
xist at different levels, and all of the levels don=E2=80=99t communicate w=
ith one another. But the movie is a hypothesis, and the hypothesis is that =
there is no better pathway to self-realization and the ennoblement of being=
 than to posit the highest good that you can conceive of and commit yoursel=
f to it. And then you might also ask yourself=E2=80=94and this is definitel=
y worth asking=E2=80=94do you really have anything better to do? And if you=
 don=E2=80=99t, why would you do anything else?<input class=3D"spoilerbutto=
