 clinical practice, I observe=E2=80=94this is also the case with my student=
s=E2=80=94that people=E2=80=99s lives aren=E2=80=99t what they would like t=
hem to be. So then you ask, why? Well, forget about tragedy and catastrophe=
. That=E2=80=99s self-evident. We=E2=80=99re not going to discuss that, alt=
hough the degree to which you bring about your own tragedy is always indete=
rminate. But I would never say that every terrible thing that is visited on=
 a person is something they deserve. I think that=E2=80=99s a very dangerou=
s presupposition, especially because everyone gets sick and dies.
<br><br>One of the main reasons that people don=E2=80=99t get what they wan=
t is because they don=E2=80=99t actually figure out what it is. And the pro=
bability that you=E2=80=99re going to get what would be good for you, let=
=E2=80=99s say=E2=80=94which would even be better than what you want. You m=
ight be wrong about what you want, easily. But maybe you could get what wou=
ld really be good for you. Well, why don=E2=80=99t you? Well, because you d=
on=E2=80=99t try. You don=E2=80=99t think, ok, here=E2=80=99s what I would =
like if I could have it. I don=E2=80=99t mean in a way that you manipulate =
the world to force it to deliver you goods or status, or something like tha=
t. That isn=E2=80=99t what I mean. I mean, something like, imagine that you=
 were taking care of yourself like you were someone you actually cared for.=
 And then you thought, ok, I=E2=80=99m caring for this person. I would like=
 for things to go as well for them as possible. What would their life have =
to be like in order for that to be the case?
<br><br>People don=E2=80=99t do that. They don=E2=80=99t sit down and think=
, all right, let=E2=80=99s figure it out. You=E2=80=99ve got a life that=E2=
=80=99s hard, obviously. Three years from now you can have what you need. Y=
ou got to be careful about it. You can=E2=80=99t have everything. You can h=
ave what would be good for you, but you have to figure out what it is. And =
then you have to aim at it. Well, my experience with people has been that, =
if they figure out what it is that would be good for them, and then they ai=
m at it, then they get it.=20
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s a strange thing. It=E2=80=99s not that simple. You may=
 formulate an idea about what would be good for you, and then you take 10 s=
teps towards that, and then you find out that your formulation was a bit of=
f, so you have to reformulate your goal. You=E2=80=99re kind of zigzagging =
as you move towards the goal. But a huge part of the reason that people fai=
l is because they don=E2=80=99t ever set up the criteria for success. And s=
o, since success is a very narrow line and very unlikely, the probability t=
hat you=E2=80=99re going to stumble on it randomly is zero. And so there=E2=
=80=99s a proposition, here. The proposition is, if you actually want somet=
hing, you can have it. The question, then, would be, well, what do you mean=
 by actually want? And the answer is that you reorient your life in every p=
ossible way to make the probability that that will occur as certain as poss=
ible.=20
<br><br>That=E2=80=99s a sacrificial idea, right? You don=E2=80=99t get eve=
rything. Obviously. But maybe you can have what you need. And maybe all you=
 have to do to get it is ask. But asking isn=E2=80=99t a whim, or today=E2=
=80=99s wish: you have to be deadly serious about it. You have to think, ok=
, I=E2=80=99m taking stock of myself. If I was going to live properly in th=
e world, and if I was going to set myself up such that being would justify =
itself in my estimation=E2=80=94and I don=E2=80=99t mean as a harsh judge=
=E2=80=94exactly what is it that I would aim at? Well, one of the things I=
=E2=80=99ve found is that=E2=80=94in test of this theory, let=E2=80=99s say=
=E2=80=A6You could try this. This is a form of prayer. Sit on your bed one =
day and ask yourself, what remarkably stupid things am I doing on a regular=
 basis to absolutely screw up my life? And if you actually ask the question=
=E2=80=94but you have to want to know the answer, right? That=E2=80=99s act=
ually what asking the question means. It doesn=E2=80=99t mean just mouthing=
 the words. It means you have to decide that you want to know. You=E2=80=99=
ll figure that out so fast that it=E2=80=99ll make your hair curl.
<br><br><a id=3D"C5"></a><div align=3D"middle"><a id=3D"C5"><span class=3D"=
