<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is =
the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction."
<br><br>Well, who in the world could possibly argue with that? Everyone in =
their right mind knows that there=E2=80=99s a million ways of doing things =
wrong. There=E2=80=99s one way, if you=E2=80=99re lucky, to do things right=
. And so the notion that it=E2=80=99s a very, very narrow pathway that you =
tread up if you=E2=80=99re doing things right=E2=80=94that=E2=80=99s wisdom=
. That=E2=80=99s the line between chaos and order that you=E2=80=99re suppo=
sed to be on, constantly. It=E2=80=99s a very, very thin line. If you=E2=80=
=99re a little bit too far in one direction, then it=E2=80=99s too much cha=
os, and if you're a little too far in the other direction, then it=E2=80=99=
s too much order. Both of those aren=E2=80=99t good. The balance has to be =
exactly right. You can feel that. I truly believe you can feel that, and I =
think it=E2=80=99s your deepest instinct. I mean that biologically; I don=
=E2=80=99t mean that metaphorically. I think that your psyche is arranged t=
o exist in a cosmos that=E2=80=99s composed of chaos and order. I think tha=
t=E2=80=99s why you have the hemispheric structure that you have. This is d=
eeper than metaphor.
<br><br>When you feel as if you=E2=80=99re meaningfully engaged in the worl=
d, when the terror of your mortality strips away, when you=E2=80=99re engag=
ed, and it=E2=80=99s timeless, that=E2=80=99s the deepest instinct that you=
 have, telling you that you=E2=80=99re in the right place at the right time=
. And then what you do is practice being there. That narrow spot that=E2=80=
=99s so difficult to find=E2=80=94you wander around it. Maybe, if you=E2=80=
=99re lucky, you can watch. This is an experiment. Watch yourself for two w=
eeks like you don=E2=80=99t know who you are, because you don=E2=80=99t. No=
tice that there=E2=80=99s gonna be times when things array properly for you=
. It=E2=80=99s not easy to notice, because, when they=E2=80=99re arrayed li=
ke that, you=E2=80=99re so engaged that you don=E2=80=99t exactly notice. B=
ut you=E2=80=99ll say, I=E2=80=99m in the right place. How did I get here? =
What am I doing right? How is it that this could happen more often? I=E2=80=
=99d like this to happen more often. How would I have to conduct myself for=
 that to happen more often? And then you practice that. Maybe, instead of 1=
0 minutes a month or 10 minutes a week, it=E2=80=99s like 15 minutes a day,=
