<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>"Because strait is the gate, and narrow is th=
e way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it. Beware of fa=
lse prophets, which come to you in sheep=E2=80=99s clothing, but inwardly t=
hey are ravening wolves." That=E2=80=99s particularly good advice for today=
=E2=80=99s political situation, I can tell you. "Ye shall know them by thei=
r fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles? Even so ever=
y good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth ev=
il fruit." Well, that=E2=80=99s what I learned from studying the history of=
 totalitarianism in the 20th century: that a corrupt tree brings forth evil=
 fruit, and that=E2=80=99s for sure.
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s so funny. People think about their relationship with d=
ivinity and God in a primitive and childish way. Why can=E2=80=99t a miracl=
e just manifest itself, so that I would be convinced? The funny thing is, f=
irst of all, you wouldn=E2=80=99t be. If a miracle actually happened, you w=
ould actually forget about it in about six months. You think that=E2=80=99s=
 not true, but it=E2=80=99s true. You would actually forget about it, becau=
se that=E2=80=99s what people are like. But there are negative miracles tha=
t are happening all the time, which actually lends some credence to my supp=
osition. You don=E2=80=99t pay any attention to that. If we can=E2=80=99t l=
earn from what happened in the 20th century, then we=E2=80=99re absolutely =
incapable of learning. What happened in the 20th century was as bitter a se=
t of lessons as you could possibly imagine.
<br><br>It=E2=80=99s associated precisely with this: "a corrupt tree bringe=
th forth evil fruit. A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can=
 a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit. Every tree that bringeth not forth =
good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire."
<br><br>Well, that=E2=80=99s a flood motif, right there: the constant arche=
type of the tree. That=E2=80=99s the archetype of being. It=E2=80=99s the a=
rchetype of the Self, often. What=E2=80=99s the warning, here? If you=E2=80=
=99re mostly deadwood, you=E2=80=99re going to burn up. You can think about=
 that metaphysically. You can project that into eternity, and you think abo=
ut that as a form of hell. The funny is that, when that=E2=80=99s happening=
 to you in realtime, it is like an eternity in hell. It=E2=80=99s a perfect=
ly reasonable way of thinking about it, but you can strip the metaphysical =
elements off, and you can say, well, if you=E2=80=99re mostly deadwood, the=
n a spark will light you on fire. That=E2=80=99s also very much worth think=
