<div class=3D"clearfix"></div>"Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them=
. Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of h=
eaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven."=20
<br><br>That=E2=80=99s an interesting line, I think. One of the proper crit=
iques of traditional Christianity=E2=80=94this is the sort of critique that=
 Nietzsche put forward=E2=80=94was that Christianity had degenerated in its=
 moral mission. Jung was a little bit more sympathetic, and I=E2=80=99ll te=
ll you why in a minute. Nietzsche=E2=80=99s idea was that Christianity had =
lost its way when it generated the presupposition that humanity was saved, =
in some final sense, by the sacrifice of Christ. It meant that the work was=
